    <string name="perf_cpu_estimate_why">Why is this an estimate?</string>
    <string name="perf_cpu_estimate_why_title">Why CPU usage is an estimate</string>
    <string name="perf_cpu_estimate_why_body">Since Android 8, the system blocks apps from reading global CPU statistics (/proc/stat), so no app from Play can measure exact system-wide CPU usage.\n\nSysMon instead estimates load from each core\'s live clock speed: a core running near its maximum frequency is treated as busy, one near its minimum as idle. This tracks real load trends well, but it is an approximation — short spikes can be missed and light background work can be over- or under-stated.\n\nThe Source stat shows which method this device uses. When a value can\'t be measured, SysMon shows “—” instead of inventing a number.</string>
    <string name="perf_cpu_unavailable_title">CPU statistics unavailable</string>
    <string name="perf_cpu_unavailable_body">This device does not expose CPU utilization or per-core frequencies to apps.</string>
